🧠 Unsupervised Learning
Unsupervised learning is the process of finding insights, patterns, or groupings within a dataset.
It works only with independent variables or (X data), without labeled outputs.


📊 Types of Unsupervised Learning:
- K-Means Clustering
- Hierarchical Clustering
- PCA (Principal Component Analysis)
- DB Scan
- TSNE (Visualization)


PCA (Principal Component Analysis)

   - It is nothing but process of reducing high dimensional to  low dimension data (Columns)
   -

NOTE:
    To reduce number of features

1.  Why should we reduce the number of features
    1.1 This is to solve the problem of "curse of dimensionality"
    1.2 This is to address multi collinearity (when columns are highly correlated to each other ). So PCA creates
        Un-Correlated features Ex:
                If columns like "house_price" , "No_f_bedrooms","No_of_restroom" is part of your input data then
                this what is called collinearity

2.  How PCA works?
    Step 1: House_Price will be in rupees , no_of_bed_rooms, no_of_rest_room will be in single digit integer. so all the
            three input are in different scale. so we have to standardize or normalize it

          Note: If you don't standardize housing_price column will take higher variance

    Step 2: Each of the column ["house_price" , "No_f_bedrooms","No_of_restroom"] will be transformed
    to have mean(Avg) of 0 under standard deviation of 1.






